{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>When the sun sets.</b> If it is a night garment, and if it is a day garment — return it in the morning. And it is already written in אֵלֶּה הַמִּשְׁפָּטִים (Exodus 22): ״עַד בֹּא הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ תְּשִׁיבֶנּוּ לוֹ״ — all day you return it to him, and when the sun sets you take it." "<b>And he blesses you.</b> And if he does not bless you, in any case — <b>and it shall be for you righteousness</b> (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:13.342121199Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}